=== S3  I13: light surface, Killing horizon, surface gravity (symbolic) ===
  [PASS] S3.0 pattern-frame inverse metric: g^ss=-1/alpha^2, g^sz=b/alpha^2, g^zz=1-b^2/alpha^2
  [PASS] S3.1 on S (alpha^2 = b^2): |dF|^2 = F_r^2 + F_phi^2/r^2 >= 0, so S is null exactly where its transverse gradient vanishes, timelike elsewhere
  [PASS] S3.2 on S the Killing covector is xi_m = (0, b, 0, 0), i.e. proportional to d zeta; it is normal to S iff F_r = F_phi = 0
  [PASS] S3.3 on S: xi^n nabla_n xi^m = kappa xi^m with a^zeta = 0
  [PASS] S3.4 signed kappa = d_zeta(alpha - b) for b = +alpha > 0 (and -d_zeta(alpha - |b|) for b = -alpha)
  [PASS] S3.5 kappa^2 = -1/2 (nabla xi)^2 = (d_zeta(alpha - b))^2 on S
  [PASS] S3.6 where the lab shift vanishes (b = v, B' = 0): kappa = d_zeta alpha
  [PASS] S3.7 stationary surface F(x)=0: g^{mn}F_mF_n = |grad F|^2 (1 - (b N_zeta)^2/alpha^2): null iff |b.N| = alpha, timelike iff |b.N| < alpha
  [PASS] S3.8 a null ray with p_perp = 0 has zero pattern-frame velocity iff b = alpha (with p_zeta along b)  (v_zeta = P*(A - B)/A)
  [PASS] S3.9 there the transverse force is -(P^2/alpha) d_perp(alpha - b): a ray rests in position and direction only where d_perp(alpha^2 - b^2) = 0, i.e. at the null points of S  (longitudinal force -P**2*(a_zeta - b_zeta)/A (the blueshift))

